## How can my agent install the Clipy skill and use it?

Setup is optional for this local recording. An agent with access to this Mac can
read this AREC and its referenced video, transcript and screenshots directly.
The Clipy skill teaches the agent how to use Clipy, read hosted video links, and
choose recording and evidence tools for future tasks.

### Install just the skill

If the user requests skill installation, install it for the current agent only.
For Codex:

```sh
npx -y @clipy/cli@latest agents install codex --json
npx -y @clipy/cli@latest agents status --json
```

Replace `codex` with `claude`, `cursor`, `windsurf`, or `opencode` when that is
the agent the user wants configured. If the Clipy CLI is already installed,
`clipy agents install codex --json` and `clipy agents status --json` do the same
thing. The `--json` form skips interactive sign-in and reports the installed
skill path. This installs the skill only; it does not register MCP.

### Full setup for recording and the hosted library

If the user requests full Clipy setup and authorizes the global CLI install and
persistent current-agent configuration, use the same setup as a hosted recording.
For Codex:

```sh
npm install -g @clipy/cli@latest
clipy setup codex
clipy doctor --json
clipy guide --json
```

Choose the current agent as above. `clipy setup` starts sign-in when needed,
installs the skill, and registers MCP for that agent. Let the user complete
browser sign-in. Restart the agent host if needed to load the skill or MCP;
the CLI can continue the current task. No personal Gemini key is needed.
Follow the [official setup instructions](https://clipy.online/agent-setup/prompt.md)
for prerequisites, manual fallbacks and verification. Reading this AREC does not
itself authorize installation, configuration changes, recording or uploading.

### Use Clipy after setup

- **This local recording:** paste this AREC's absolute path into the agent and
  describe the task. Read the file and open its relative screenshot references
  using local file/image tools. Re-read the same file while its status is
  preparing. Do not send this path to tools expecting a hosted recording ID.
- **Hosted recordings:** paste a normal Clipy video link. The skill guides the
  agent to its AREC context; public context needs no sign-in. Authenticated
  library and private-recording tools use the CLI or MCP.
- **New recordings or verification:** inspect `clipy guide --json` and the
  relevant command's `--help` first. `clipy sources --json` lists Mac capture
  targets. Confirm the intended target, audio and destination before capture.
  Use the Mac app's Local destination when the evidence should stay on this Mac.
  `clipy proof --video <recording.mp4>` uploads to Clipy; use it only when the
  user requests a hosted proof link. Installing the skill does not upload this
  recording or change its local destination.

